nl.statement:
For each library depth \(m\), let \(\mathscr C_m\) be a finite deterministic library of rational circles, increasing with \(m\).  On prespecified independent folds, form the empirical transforms \(\widehat F_{a,n}\), \(\widehat G_{a,n}\), and their derivatives.  For a circle \(C=\{\rho e^{it}:0\le t\le2\pi\}\) on which the empirical denominator is certified positive, the candidate record may contain only quantities definitionally computed from the actual empirical contour integrands
\[
 W_{a,C}(t)=\rho e^{it}
 \frac{\widehat F'_{a,n}(\rho e^{it})}
      {\widehat F_{a,n}(\rho e^{it})},
 \qquad
 V_{a,C}(t)=\rho e^{it}
 \frac{\widehat G_{a,n}(\rho e^{it})}
      {\widehat F_{a,n}(\rho e^{it})}.
\]
Specifically, it may record the boundary modulus \(\inf_{z\in C}|\widehat F_{a,n}(z)|\), the winding enclosure for \((2\pi)^{-1}\int_0^{2\pi}W_{a,C}(t)\,dt\), the contour-moment enclosure for \((2\pi)^{-1}\int_0^{2\pi}V_{a,C}(t)\,dt\), and the angular variance
\[
 \widehat v_{a,C}
 =\frac1{2\pi}\int_0^{2\pi}
 \left|V_{a,C}(t)-
 \frac1{2\pi}\int_0^{2\pi}V_{a,C}(u)\,du\right|^2dt.
\]
These records constitute candidate data only.  No rule selecting among DML, finite-order ACE, and contour moments, no contribution formula beyond the displayed empirical integrands, no argmin or tie-breaking prescription, and no risk, coverage, critical-scaling, or lower-bound guarantee is defined.  The symbol \(\widehat\theta_{\mathrm{ad}}\) is reserved for a future estimator satisfying the desiderata in \(\text{oeq:local-to-gaussian-frontier}\); that estimator and its performance are unresolved.

nl.frozen_body:
Fix a parameter tuple with positive sample size \(n\), fixed ACE order \(r\ge2\), cumulant order \(k=r+1\), \(s\ge r\), \(\gamma\in(1/2,1)\), strictly positive \(C_\theta,C_g,C_q,\psi_\eta,\psi_\xi,\delta,\sigma\), and nonnegative nonincreasing sequences \(\epsilon_{1n}\) and \(\epsilon_{2n}\) on positive indices. Work on a measurable covariate space with observations \(O=(X,T,Y)\), and fix a probability law \(P\) with real functional \(\theta_0(P)\), measurable conditional means \(g_0(X)=E_P[T\mid X]\) and \(q_0(X)=E_P[Y\mid X]\), integrable \(T\) and \(Y\), and deterministic measurable supplied regression-code sequences for treatment and outcome.

For each library depth \(d\), let \(\mathscr C_d\) be the deterministic finite library of rational circles represented by the positive rational radii \(\rho=j+1\), \(0\le j<d\). For a realized sample indexed by \(\{0,\ldots,n-1\}\), form the empirical transforms \(\widehat F_{a,n}\) and \(\widehat G_{a,n}\) on the prespecified deterministic fold \(a\in\{0,1\}\), using indices below \(n/2\) for \(a=0\) and indices at least \(n/2\) for \(a=1\). For a circle \(C\in\mathscr C_d\), \(C=\{\rho e^{it}:0\le t\le2\pi\}\), on which the empirical boundary modulus is certified positive, the candidate record consists of quantities definitionally computed from the empirical contour integrands
\[
 W_{a,C}(t)=\rho e^{it}
 \frac{\widehat F'_{a,n}(\rho e^{it})}
      {\widehat F_{a,n}(\rho e^{it})},
 \qquad
 V_{a,C}(t)=\rho e^{it}
 \frac{\widehat G_{a,n}(\rho e^{it})}
      {\widehat F_{a,n}(\rho e^{it})}.
\]
Specifically, the record contains a rational interval enclosure of the boundary modulus \(\inf_{z\in C}|\widehat F_{a,n}(z)|\), a complex rational interval enclosure for \((2\pi)^{-1}\int_0^{2\pi}W_{a,C}(t)\,dt\), a complex rational interval enclosure for \((2\pi)^{-1}\int_0^{2\pi}V_{a,C}(t)\,dt\), and a rational interval enclosure of the angular variance
\[
 \widehat v_{a,C}
 =\frac1{2\pi}\int_0^{2\pi}
 \left|V_{a,C}(t)-
 \frac1{2\pi}\int_0^{2\pi}V_{a,C}(u)\,du\right|^2dt.
\]
Each enclosure is accompanied by its soundness certificate for the displayed empirical quantity, and the actual empirical transforms on the stated deterministic fold are the transform inputs of the schema. These records are candidate data for one realized sample, one deterministic inference fold, and one rational circle.

nl.statement:
If \(\mathsf E_n^{\mathrm{JMS}}\) holds and \(\varepsilon_{1,n},\varepsilon_{2,n}>0\), Jin--Mackey--Syrgkanis Theorem 5.4 gives, on \(\mathcal P_{\mathrm{ACE},n}^{\mathrm{JMS}}\),
\[
 \begin{aligned}
 &\sup_{P\in\mathcal P_{\mathrm{ACE},n}^{\mathrm{JMS}}}
 Q_{P,1-\gamma}(|\widehat\theta_{\mathrm{ACE},r,n}-\theta_0(P)|)\\
 &\quad\le C_{\gamma}r!16^r\delta^{-1}
 \Big[\varepsilon_{1,n}^r\varepsilon_{2,n}
 +C_{\theta}\varepsilon_{1,n}^{r+1}
 +64(C_g+\psi_{\eta})^r
 \{r^2(C_g+\psi_{\eta})+\psi_{\xi}+C_{\theta}\psi_{\eta}\}
 (\gamma n)^{-1/2}\Big].
 \end{aligned}
\]

In the notation of \(\text{def:jms-ace-class}\) and
\(\text{def:jms-eligibility}\), Jin--Mackey--Syrgkanis Theorem 5.4
states that, whenever \(\mathsf E_n^{\mathrm{JMS}}\) holds and
\(\varepsilon_{1,n},\varepsilon_{2,n}>0\),
\[
\begin{split}
 &\sup_{P\in\mathcal P_{\mathrm{ACE},n}^{\mathrm{JMS}}}
 Q_{P,1-\gamma}
 \!\left(|\widehat\theta_{\mathrm{ACE},r,n}-\theta_0(P)|\right)\\
 &\quad\le C_\gamma r!16^r\delta^{-1}
 \Bigl[\varepsilon_{1,n}^r\varepsilon_{2,n}
 +C_\theta\varepsilon_{1,n}^{r+1}
 +64(C_g+\psi_\eta)^r
 \{r^2(C_g+\psi_\eta)+\psi_\xi+C_\theta\psi_\eta\}
 (\gamma n)^{-1/2}\Bigr].
\end{split}
\]

For every \(n\) and every \(P\in\mathcal P_{\mathrm G,n}^{\mathrm{JMS}}\), the simultaneous restrictions in \(\text{def:gaussian-class}\) imply \(\theta_0(P)=0\). If \(\mathcal P_{\mathrm G,n}^{\mathrm{JMS}}\neq\varnothing\), then the zero statistic is minimax and
\[
 \mathfrak R_n^{\mathrm G}
 =\mathfrak M_{n,1-\gamma}^{\mathrm G}
 =0.
\]
